1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:12,420
Slide 11 delivers our first major 실전 사례: "CASE STUDY 1: 24/7 LOGISTICS AUTOPILOT: How a Global Freight Carrier Eliminated Overnight Cargo Delays."

2
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:20,458
Listen to this nightmare, students: this global shipping line operates between Shanghai, Rotterdam, and Los Angeles.

3
00:00:20,458 --> 00:00:29,690
Every single night between 1:00 AM and 5:00 AM, 1,200 emails containing messy PDF bills of lading and customs declarations flooded their shared inbox!

4
00:00:30,590 --> 00:00:33,760
And what did their night shift do, James?

5
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:45,509
Three exhausted junior dispatchers sat there drinking cold coffee, manually opening PDFs, retyping 14-digit container numbers into a 1995 legacy ERP system!

6
00:00:45,509 --> 00:00:51,700
If they made one typo, an entire $200,000 container was held up at the port for 48 hours!

7
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:57,706
Look at the 3-phase Spark architecture on screen that solved this!

8
00:00:57,706 --> 00:01:03,044
Phase 1: A headless Gmail webhook intercepts every incoming document.

9
00:01:03,044 --> 00:01:12,020
Phase 2: Gemini 3.5 Flash extracts container IDs, hazardous cargo codes, and arrival timestamps in 350 milliseconds!

10
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:18,029
And Phase 3: The agent auto-cleared 94% of standard cargo directly into the ERP!

11
00:01:18,029 --> 00:01:27,800
But if an import had an expired fumigation certificate or chemical mismatch, the agent flagged it in red and pings the senior customs officer at 6:00 AM!

12
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:37,270
Result: Port document processing time dropped by 92%, and zero containers missed their feeder vessel due to lost paperwork!

13
00:01:38,170 --> 00:01:42,675
That is persistent cloud autonomy in enterprise action.

14
00:01:42,675 --> 00:01:46,690
Now let us step inside the engine room in Part 2!

